\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Execution variability on shared A100 GPUs. (a) Radio p99 of a two-cell 273-PRB PUSCH pipeline against the MPS share of a co-running Qwen prefill class: one 16-token request (light) or eight 512-token requests (heavy). Lines connect run means, and bars span the runs. (b) Complementary CDF of latency normalized by its median: host construction of a scheduling certificate (1,200 periods), cross-GPU receiver pairs at the 4.5\nonbreakingspace ms scale with a Python and a partly native C++/CUDA path (1,000 and 300 slots), and the NeuralRx\xspace  TensorRT graph (300 slots).}}{4}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:execution}{{3}{4}{Execution variability on shared A100 GPUs. (a) Radio p99 of a two-cell 273-PRB PUSCH pipeline against the MPS share of a co-running Qwen prefill class: one 16-token request (light) or eight 512-token requests (heavy). Lines connect run means, and bars span the runs. (b) Complementary CDF of latency normalized by its median: host construction of a scheduling certificate (1,200 periods), cross-GPU receiver pairs at the 4.5~ms scale with a Python and a partly native C++/CUDA path (1,000 and 300 slots), and the \NRx TensorRT graph (300 slots)}{figure.caption.5}{}}
